domain AgencyContractDetail:
  description "Detail the accepted agency requirements and preserve Seal evidence."
problem P1:
  |
    Requirement revision 1 is accepted; concrete provenance, reaction projection,
    writer lifetime, failure precedence, activation and accounting remain to specify.
evidence E1:
  |
    Exact accepted requirement hash is
    f733f85a153349e4be28785fef05d93006d057e0e5d507a8423b658f9bb7f444.
    Separate acceptance record preserves original bytes. Independent review completed.
evidence E2:
  |
    Current free-action defaultObjective has no provenance; OpenAI authoring prompts
    can generate victory defaults in an existing decisionProfile. Presence is not
    author-explicit evidence. Reaction policy already returns bounded action and
    expression projections. Dialogue settings writer currently pins schemaVersion 2.
evidence E3:
  |
    The matching checkout is 0754ca7, origin/main 1cdf210, ahead21 behind0 with prior
    WIP. ADR0028 is locally unallocated. This checkout lacks template.think and
    npm adr:check, while the primary checkout has the template and a checker that
    scans only its own directory. Do not claim that checker validates this worktree.
premise AUTHORITY:
  |
    Owner requested concrete design and Seal. Accepted requirements and ADR0027
    constrain it; new ADR remains Proposed. No runtime implementation, paid call,
    push or deployment. Preserve accepted requirement bytes and existing ADRs.
premise OPTIONS:
  |
    A infer author intent from profile presence or wording, rejected as ambiguous.
    B freeze explicit owner-confirmed objective provenance in a new character asset
    generation content contract, retain V2 definition, and block ambiguous V3 start
    until resolved; no separate database or tactical planner.
    C silently call unknown provenance absent, rejected because explicit intent
    might be erased. For reaction, reuse bounded projections rather than raw state.
pending LIMITS:
  |
    New contract adoption and details require owner approval; actual model quality
    and provider budgets remain unverified. Existing ADR checker is unavailable in
    this worktree; direct CLI audits and projection checks must be labeled separately.
decision D1 based_on P1, E1, E2, AUTHORITY, OPTIONS, LIMITS:
  |
    Draft ADR0028 using B, explicit frozen provenance and unknown-start failure,
    one conscious provider result per normal slot, existing bounded reaction
    projections and no extra deliberative psyche call. Specify old-field inert
    states, closed outputs, typed partial acceptance, later fallback and private
    state boundaries. Keep V1/V2 routes and immutable snapshots intact.
decision D2 based_on D1, E3, AUTHORITY, LIMITS:
  |
    Use the repository Markdown template and read the primary think template as
    an authoring reference without modifying that checkout. Audit the proposed
    canonical think via installed CLI before relying on it. Attempt required
    npm adr:check and report its absence; do not install unrelated governance tooling.
decision D3 based_on D1, D2, AUTHORITY:
  |
    Inspect Seal status and impact before changing registered plans. Register
    independent review and exact requirement acceptance as distinct evidence, keep
    the requirement seal immutable, add Proposed ADR and projection, update reviewed
    design/backlog/PERT to the ADR gate, and reseal each verified dependency only.
    Record digest, stale scan and fsck. Stop before implementation and ADR acceptance.
